# Review: MeetingPlugin

The four operations exist and do roughly what the spec says: `Create` builds the meeting with a fresh
Transcript and empty notes and summary Texts, `SetActive` updates state and the call activity,
`HandlePayload` resolves the meeting and feed, and `Summarize` delegates to
`TranscriptOperation.Summarize` and writes `meeting.summary`. None of them has a test; the only test is
module activation, and the story play functions that touch meetings are tagged `!test`.

The biggest finding is that the call lifecycle is dead code. `call-extension.ts` contributes
`CallsCapabilities.EventHandler` (`onJoin`, `onLeave`, `onCallStateUpdated`, `onMediaStateUpdated`),
but nothing in plugin-calls or elsewhere reads that capability, so the TranscriptionManager is never
opened on join, never fed speaking state, and `HandlePayload` is never triggered from call state; the
module's own comment notes `onJoin` is never invoked. Other divergences: the `Meeting` type has no
`created` field, `MeetingArticle` is a tabbed hub (notes / transcript / summary / call) rather than a
side-by-side view, the summary uses a Sonnet model rather than Haiku, `MeetingsList` sorts by label
rather than newest-first, and the `entityExtraction` setting (F-6) does not exist — `Settings` is an
empty struct.

